    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d17">

                <pb facs="0061" n="15" sameAs="frus:frus1914-20v02/pg15"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">763.72/4525½</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">President Wilson to the
                            Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1917-05-07">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">7 May, 1917</hi>
                        </date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">My Dear Mr. Secretary</hi>: The practicability and
                    wisdom of carrying out this very useful suggestion depends, as in so many other
                    cases, upon finding the right man,—a really capable man who will be equally able
                    and well poised and sensible, not likely to swell with importance and instruct
                    us every day by cable. Have you such a man in mind, or do you think you could
                    find one?</p>
                <p>Faithfully Yours,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>W. W.</signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
